1
00:00:00,295 --> 00:00:01,950
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:01,950 --> 00:00:04,083
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:04,842 --> 00:00:05,900
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,316 --> 00:00:07,125
I had my right knee

5
00:00:07,125 --> 00:00:08,751
replaced two years ago.

6
00:00:08,751 --> 00:00:10,749
It has hurt every day
since.

7
00:00:10,749 --> 00:00:12,280
Not surgery pain.

8
00:00:12,280 --> 00:00:13,393
I know what that felt
like,

9
00:00:13,393 --> 00:00:14,706
and it went away.

10
00:00:14,706 --> 00:00:15,866
This is different.

11
00:00:15,866 --> 00:00:16,770
Tight.

12
00:00:16,770 --> 00:00:17,807
Full.

13
00:00:17,807 --> 00:00:18,749
Like a band around

14
00:00:18,749 --> 00:00:20,756
the joint that never
loosens.

15
00:00:20,756 --> 00:00:21,783
And for two years I've

16
00:00:21,783 --> 00:00:23,381
been told the same thing.

17
00:00:23,381 --> 00:00:24,484
Give it time.

18
00:00:24,484 --> 00:00:26,368
At six weeks it was
swelling,

19
00:00:26,368 --> 00:00:28,061
and swelling is normal.

20
00:00:28,061 --> 00:00:29,126
At three months,

21
00:00:29,126 --> 00:00:30,163
give it six.

22
00:00:30,163 --> 00:00:31,267
At six months,

23
00:00:31,267 --> 00:00:32,925
some knees take a full
year.

24
00:00:33,597 --> 00:00:34,425
At a year,

25
00:00:34,425 --> 00:00:36,498
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

26
00:00:36,498 --> 00:00:37,802
And I didn't just wait.

27
00:00:37,802 --> 00:00:39,133
We went down the list.

28
00:00:39,133 --> 00:00:40,608
More physical therapy.

29
00:00:40,608 --> 00:00:41,559
Every session,

30
00:00:41,559 --> 00:00:43,090
every exercise at home.

31
00:00:43,090 --> 00:00:44,099
I got stronger.

32
00:00:44,099 --> 00:00:45,849
The tightness never moved.

33
00:00:45,849 --> 00:00:47,590
The pain pills helped,

34
00:00:47,590 --> 00:00:49,178
and that was the problem.

35
00:00:49,178 --> 00:00:51,385
I'm already on enough
every morning,

36
00:00:51,385 --> 00:00:52,393
and nobody could tell me

37
00:00:52,393 --> 00:00:53,687
when I'd get to stop.

38
00:00:53,687 --> 00:00:55,380
Then a nerve block.

39
00:00:55,380 --> 00:00:57,559
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

40
00:00:57,559 --> 00:00:59,280
And after that, a second

41
00:00:59,280 --> 00:01:00,374
operation to go back

42
00:01:00,374 --> 00:01:02,505
in and do it over.

43
00:01:02,505 --> 00:01:03,799
I said no.

44
00:01:03,799 --> 00:01:06,081
Every morning I stepped
out of bed

45
00:01:06,081 --> 00:01:07,042
and my knee felt like

46
00:01:07,042 --> 00:01:08,859
a band was wrapped around
it,

47
00:01:08,859 --> 00:01:11,325
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

48
00:01:11,722 --> 00:01:13,282
Every morning I took
something

49
00:01:13,282 --> 00:01:14,291
for it and got

50
00:01:14,291 --> 00:01:15,480
on with my day.

51
00:01:15,480 --> 00:01:16,735
Couldn't do the stairs,

52
00:01:16,735 --> 00:01:17,772
couldn't stand at the
counter

53
00:01:17,772 --> 00:01:19,246
long enough to finish
dinner,

54
00:01:19,246 --> 00:01:20,863
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's game

55
00:01:20,863 --> 00:01:22,680
without shifting every two
minutes.

56
00:01:22,680 --> 00:01:23,860
It woke me at night,

57
00:01:23,860 --> 00:01:25,724
and it turned ordinary
things,

58
00:01:25,724 --> 00:01:26,809
like getting in the car

59
00:01:26,809 --> 00:01:28,102
or up off the couch,

60
00:01:28,102 --> 00:01:29,284
into a decision.

61
00:01:29,824 --> 00:01:31,232
After a long and serious

62
00:01:31,232 --> 00:01:32,583
talk with my husband,

63
00:01:32,583 --> 00:01:34,514
I went back in one more
time.

64
00:01:34,514 --> 00:01:35,607
That was the fourth set

65
00:01:35,607 --> 00:01:37,301
of X-rays on this knee.

66
00:01:37,301 --> 00:01:38,899
And like the three before
it,

67
00:01:38,899 --> 00:01:41,565
the answer was everything
looks great.

68
00:01:42,066 --> 00:01:44,235
No loosening, no
infection,

69
00:01:44,235 --> 00:01:45,329
nothing wrong.

70
00:01:45,329 --> 00:01:46,394
Only this time

71
00:01:46,394 --> 00:01:48,154
there was no new number.

72
00:01:48,154 --> 00:01:50,732
Nobody said give it
another six months.

73
00:01:50,732 --> 00:01:52,520
There was nothing left to
give it.

74
00:01:52,520 --> 00:01:53,376
I sat in the parking

75
00:01:53,376 --> 00:01:54,492
lot for a while.

76
00:01:55,288 --> 00:01:56,991
Okay, I thought.

77
00:01:56,991 --> 00:01:58,465
Then explain this.

78
00:01:58,465 --> 00:02:00,739
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

79
00:02:00,739 --> 00:02:02,156
I hit my breaking point.

80
00:02:02,156 --> 00:02:04,325
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

81
00:02:04,325 --> 00:02:05,980
Everyone in the house was
asleep

82
00:02:05,980 --> 00:02:07,530
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

83
00:02:07,530 --> 00:02:08,634
with my leg up,

84
00:02:08,634 --> 00:02:09,890
trying to find any angle

85
00:02:09,890 --> 00:02:11,069
where it didn't feel like
something

86
00:02:11,069 --> 00:02:13,333
was wrapped around my knee
and tightening.

87
00:02:13,333 --> 00:02:15,730
My husband didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

88
00:02:15,730 --> 00:02:17,873
By then I'd stopped
telling him.

89
00:02:18,536 --> 00:02:19,582
And I just thought,

90
00:02:19,582 --> 00:02:21,190
is this really my life
now?

91
00:02:21,190 --> 00:02:22,655
I can't live like this.

92
00:02:22,655 --> 00:02:24,443
So I made myself a
promise.

93
00:02:24,443 --> 00:02:25,309
I wouldn't go a day

94
00:02:25,309 --> 00:02:27,002
without looking for an
answer.

95
00:02:27,002 --> 00:02:28,410
And when I found one,

96
00:02:28,410 --> 00:02:30,017
I'd share it with everyone

97
00:02:30,017 --> 00:02:31,406
going through the same
thing.

98
00:02:31,406 --> 00:02:32,785
So I got my laptop

99
00:02:32,785 --> 00:02:34,374
out and went looking.

100
00:02:34,374 --> 00:02:35,839
Not for a product.

101
00:02:35,839 --> 00:02:37,228
For an explanation.

102
00:02:37,228 --> 00:02:38,797
Mayo Clinic forums,

103
00:02:38,797 --> 00:02:40,902
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

104
00:02:41,365 --> 00:02:42,621
doctor videos,

105
00:02:42,621 --> 00:02:44,390
medical animations.

106
00:02:44,390 --> 00:02:45,922
And that's when I found a
video

107
00:02:45,922 --> 00:02:48,005
from a physical therapist
named Dr.

108
00:02:48,005 --> 00:02:50,221
Steven Salinger, whose own
wife

109
00:02:50,221 --> 00:02:52,314
had been through exactly
this.

110
00:02:52,314 --> 00:02:54,026
But before I say anything
else,

111
00:02:54,026 --> 00:02:55,548
I want to be straight with
you.

112
00:02:55,548 --> 00:02:57,803
You've already had
something work fast.

113
00:02:57,803 --> 00:02:58,849
The ice.

114
00:02:58,849 --> 00:03:00,488
The first week of a new
pill.

115
00:03:00,932 --> 00:03:02,797
The good day after a
session.

116
00:03:02,797 --> 00:03:04,908
Then it wore off.

117
00:03:04,908 --> 00:03:07,068
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

118
00:03:07,068 --> 00:03:09,037
Fast relief isn't relief.

119
00:03:09,037 --> 00:03:10,387
It's a preview.

120
00:03:10,387 --> 00:03:11,529
So I'm not going to tell

121
00:03:11,529 --> 00:03:12,889
you this works fast.

122
00:03:12,889 --> 00:03:13,755
It doesn't.

123
00:03:13,755 --> 00:03:15,429
But if you're willing to
be patient,

124
00:03:15,429 --> 00:03:16,161
and to look at what's

125
00:03:16,161 --> 00:03:17,873
going on around your new
knee

126
00:03:17,873 --> 00:03:19,376
instead of inside it,
there

127
00:03:19,376 --> 00:03:21,726
is a real reason it still
hurts.

128
00:03:21,726 --> 00:03:23,800
And something you can do
about it.

129
00:03:23,800 --> 00:03:25,379
Let me explain what he
said,

130
00:03:25,379 --> 00:03:26,644
because this is what
changed

131
00:03:26,644 --> 00:03:27,835
everything for me.

132
00:03:28,451 --> 00:03:30,296
He started with the
basics.

133
00:03:30,296 --> 00:03:31,799
A knee replacement takes
out

134
00:03:31,799 --> 00:03:33,454
the worn joint surfaces

135
00:03:33,454 --> 00:03:35,528
and puts in metal and
plastic.

136
00:03:35,528 --> 00:03:37,288
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

137
00:03:37,288 --> 00:03:39,079
you had before the
operation.

138
00:03:39,704 --> 00:03:41,388
That part I already knew.

139
00:03:41,388 --> 00:03:42,681
But then he explained
something

140
00:03:42,681 --> 00:03:44,546
nobody had ever told me.

141
00:03:44,546 --> 00:03:45,449
He said,

142
00:03:45,449 --> 00:03:46,715
think about a swollen foot

143
00:03:46,715 --> 00:03:48,084
inside a shoe.

144
00:03:48,084 --> 00:03:49,502
The shoe didn't shrink.

145
00:03:49,502 --> 00:03:51,499
Your foot is taking up
more room,

146
00:03:51,499 --> 00:03:53,145
so everything feels
cramped

147
00:03:53,145 --> 00:03:55,104
and tight and squeezed.

148
00:03:55,104 --> 00:03:56,208
Your new knee sits

149
00:03:56,208 --> 00:03:58,015
in a limited space with
living

150
00:03:58,015 --> 00:04:00,336
tissue packed all around
it.

151
00:04:00,336 --> 00:04:02,219
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

152
00:04:02,219 --> 00:04:04,179
had to work through that
tissue.

153
00:04:04,179 --> 00:04:07,223
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

154
00:04:07,223 --> 00:04:08,735
At first that's normal.

155
00:04:08,735 --> 00:04:09,962
But in some people

156
00:04:09,962 --> 00:04:11,503
that swelling can stay
switched

157
00:04:11,503 --> 00:04:13,482
on far longer than
expected.

158
00:04:13,482 --> 00:04:15,251
And swollen tissue takes
up more

159
00:04:15,251 --> 00:04:17,154
room than calm tissue
does.

160
00:04:17,154 --> 00:04:18,581
So when you bend,

161
00:04:18,581 --> 00:04:20,312
that tissue gets
compressed.

162
00:04:20,312 --> 00:04:21,234
When you straighten,

163
00:04:21,234 --> 00:04:22,559
it gets pulled tight.

164
00:04:23,042 --> 00:04:24,002
That's the band.

165
00:04:24,002 --> 00:04:26,133
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

166
00:04:26,133 --> 00:04:26,847
And you start being

167
00:04:26,847 --> 00:04:27,845
the one who says,

168
00:04:27,845 --> 00:04:28,711
you go ahead.

169
00:04:28,711 --> 00:04:29,853
I'll stay here.

170
00:04:29,853 --> 00:04:31,175
And that's exactly why so
much

171
00:04:31,175 --> 00:04:33,401
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

172
00:04:33,401 --> 00:04:35,560
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

173
00:04:35,560 --> 00:04:36,454
around the knee.

174
00:04:36,454 --> 00:04:37,301
Worth doing,

175
00:04:37,301 --> 00:04:38,254
and I'd done it.

176
00:04:39,051 --> 00:04:40,440
It does nothing about
tissue

177
00:04:40,440 --> 00:04:41,771
taking up room.

178
00:04:41,771 --> 00:04:43,208
A nerve block quiets

179
00:04:43,208 --> 00:04:45,357
the nerve carrying the
signal.

180
00:04:45,357 --> 00:04:47,225
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

181
00:04:47,821 --> 00:04:49,400
But when that irritated
tissue

182
00:04:49,400 --> 00:04:50,951
finally calms down,

183
00:04:50,951 --> 00:04:52,339
it holds less fluid,

184
00:04:52,339 --> 00:04:53,985
and it takes up less room.

185
00:04:53,985 --> 00:04:56,154
Less room taken up means
less pressure

186
00:04:56,154 --> 00:04:57,666
squeezing the joint.

187
00:04:57,666 --> 00:04:59,502
That's what takes the
pressure off.

188
00:04:59,502 --> 00:05:01,091
After two years of this,

189
00:05:01,091 --> 00:05:02,634
it finally made sense.

190
00:05:03,269 --> 00:05:05,219
The problem was never the
new knee.

191
00:05:05,219 --> 00:05:07,140
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

192
00:05:07,140 --> 00:05:08,719
He calls it the squeeze.

193
00:05:08,719 --> 00:05:11,012
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

194
00:05:11,012 --> 00:05:12,382
I'd bought knee sleeves,

195
00:05:12,382 --> 00:05:14,522
compression braces,
creams,

196
00:05:14,522 --> 00:05:16,158
half of Amazon really,

197
00:05:16,158 --> 00:05:17,309
and all any of it gave

198
00:05:17,309 --> 00:05:19,392
me was an hour.

199
00:05:19,392 --> 00:05:20,353
I even looked at going

200
00:05:20,353 --> 00:05:22,132
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

201
00:05:22,132 --> 00:05:24,186
But at $200 a session

202
00:05:24,186 --> 00:05:26,149
with nothing covered by
insurance,

203
00:05:26,717 --> 00:05:28,058
that was a quick no.

204
00:05:28,058 --> 00:05:29,152
Then one night I went

205
00:05:29,152 --> 00:05:30,407
back to that knee
replacement

206
00:05:30,407 --> 00:05:32,310
group and actually read
it.

207
00:05:32,310 --> 00:05:33,974
Thousands of people,

208
00:05:33,974 --> 00:05:35,642
years out from surgery,

209
00:05:36,162 --> 00:05:38,635
comparing notes on
stiffness and tightness

210
00:05:38,635 --> 00:05:40,265
nobody could explain.

211
00:05:40,709 --> 00:05:42,678
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

212
00:05:42,678 --> 00:05:44,790
the same thing kept coming
up.

213
00:05:44,790 --> 00:05:45,732
This one device,

214
00:05:45,732 --> 00:05:47,177
and people saying it was
the first

215
00:05:47,177 --> 00:05:48,655
thing that made a
difference.

216
00:05:49,318 --> 00:05:51,344
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

217
00:05:51,344 --> 00:05:52,809
alright, here it comes,

218
00:05:52,809 --> 00:05:54,378
she's selling me
something,

219
00:05:54,378 --> 00:05:56,138
let me shut that down
right now.

220
00:05:56,138 --> 00:05:57,384
I'm only here because I
made

221
00:05:57,384 --> 00:05:58,982
myself a promise at 2:30

222
00:05:58,982 --> 00:06:00,266
in the morning that if I

223
00:06:00,266 --> 00:06:02,026
ever found something that
helped,

224
00:06:02,026 --> 00:06:03,047
I'd say so.

225
00:06:03,919 --> 00:06:05,536
It's called the KenRelief
Red

226
00:06:05,536 --> 00:06:06,918
Light Therapy Wrap.

227
00:06:07,334 --> 00:06:09,598
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

228
00:06:09,598 --> 00:06:10,539
It looked like the cheap

229
00:06:10,539 --> 00:06:12,099
knee sleeves off Amazon

230
00:06:12,099 --> 00:06:13,698
that did nothing for me.

231
00:06:13,698 --> 00:06:15,448
But I went to their
website anyway,

232
00:06:15,448 --> 00:06:16,304
just to see what all

233
00:06:16,304 --> 00:06:17,607
the fuss was about.

234
00:06:17,607 --> 00:06:19,548
It's the same red light
therapy clinics

235
00:06:19,548 --> 00:06:22,487
charge $200 a session for,

236
00:06:22,487 --> 00:06:25,036
off machines that cost
fifty thousand dollars,

237
00:06:25,036 --> 00:06:25,940
in a wrap you plug

238
00:06:25,940 --> 00:06:27,233
into the wall at home.

239
00:06:27,233 --> 00:06:28,936
Two hundred and forty
lights.

240
00:06:28,936 --> 00:06:31,162
Red at 660 nanometers

241
00:06:31,162 --> 00:06:33,711
and near-infrared at 850,

242
00:06:33,711 --> 00:06:35,835
run together for the
strongest effect.

243
00:06:36,318 --> 00:06:38,020
Four strength levels.

244
00:06:38,020 --> 00:06:39,849
A five to thirty minute
timer.

245
00:06:40,313 --> 00:06:41,768
Then I saw the guarantee.

246
00:06:41,768 --> 00:06:42,767
Ninety days.

247
00:06:42,767 --> 00:06:44,422
Results or your money
back,

248
00:06:44,422 --> 00:06:46,714
no questions, no store
credit,

249
00:06:46,714 --> 00:06:48,550
and you don't even send it
back.

250
00:06:48,550 --> 00:06:50,738
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

251
00:06:50,738 --> 00:06:52,393
days to change my mind.

252
00:06:52,393 --> 00:06:53,725
There wasn't much to lose,

253
00:06:53,725 --> 00:06:54,943
so I ordered it.

254
00:06:54,943 --> 00:06:56,265
Two of them, actually.

255
00:06:56,265 --> 00:06:58,006
Only the right knee was
replaced,

256
00:06:58,006 --> 00:06:59,737
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

257
00:06:59,737 --> 00:07:01,611
and I'd done it for two
years.

258
00:07:01,611 --> 00:07:03,722
The left one was carrying
the difference.

259
00:07:03,722 --> 00:07:04,521
When it came,

260
00:07:04,521 --> 00:07:06,500
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

261
00:07:06,500 --> 00:07:07,499
because I'd been let down

262
00:07:07,499 --> 00:07:09,411
too many times to get
excited.

263
00:07:09,411 --> 00:07:10,799
What I felt was warmth.

264
00:07:10,799 --> 00:07:12,521
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

265
00:07:12,521 --> 00:07:13,948
More like it was coming
from inside

266
00:07:13,948 --> 00:07:15,641
the knee and spreading
around it.

267
00:07:15,641 --> 00:07:16,707
And that was it.

268
00:07:16,707 --> 00:07:18,390
That was the whole
experience.

269
00:07:18,390 --> 00:07:19,465
When I took it off,

270
00:07:19,465 --> 00:07:20,397
I'll be honest,

271
00:07:20,397 --> 00:07:22,138
nothing dramatic had
happened.

272
00:07:22,138 --> 00:07:23,824
And after what that video
said,

273
00:07:24,373 --> 00:07:26,361
that's exactly what I
expected.

274
00:07:26,361 --> 00:07:27,474
What was different

275
00:07:27,474 --> 00:07:28,654
was that for the first
time

276
00:07:28,654 --> 00:07:30,452
in two years I'd done
something

277
00:07:30,452 --> 00:07:32,516
for my knee instead of to
it.

278
00:07:32,516 --> 00:07:33,553
Twenty minutes,

279
00:07:33,553 --> 00:07:34,827
in my own chair.

280
00:07:34,827 --> 00:07:36,435
No drive, no copay.

281
00:07:36,435 --> 00:07:38,157
They say twenty minutes.

282
00:07:38,157 --> 00:07:39,213
I did thirty,

283
00:07:39,213 --> 00:07:40,211
twice a day,

284
00:07:40,211 --> 00:07:42,002
lowest setting that first
week.

285
00:07:42,751 --> 00:07:44,359
I put it on the calendar.

286
00:07:44,359 --> 00:07:45,395
The first week,

287
00:07:45,395 --> 00:07:46,166
I couldn't have told

288
00:07:46,166 --> 00:07:47,852
you if anything was
happening.

289
00:07:48,344 --> 00:07:49,229
I tried not to get

290
00:07:49,229 --> 00:07:50,202
my hopes up.

291
00:07:50,561 --> 00:07:51,407
I'd had things help

292
00:07:51,407 --> 00:07:53,129
for a week and then stop.

293
00:07:53,129 --> 00:07:54,851
But somewhere in the
second week I

294
00:07:54,851 --> 00:07:56,306
noticed I'd come down the
stairs

295
00:07:56,306 --> 00:07:57,669
without holding the rail.

296
00:07:58,304 --> 00:07:59,911
I hadn't decided to.

297
00:07:59,911 --> 00:08:01,500
I just did it, then
stopped

298
00:08:01,500 --> 00:08:03,887
halfway down because I
realized.

299
00:08:03,887 --> 00:08:05,457
By the end of the fourth
week

300
00:08:05,457 --> 00:08:06,570
I'd slept through the
night

301
00:08:06,570 --> 00:08:07,933
four times running.

302
00:08:08,729 --> 00:08:09,775
I stood at the counter

303
00:08:09,775 --> 00:08:10,964
and finished making dinner

304
00:08:10,964 --> 00:08:12,715
without looking for the
stool.

305
00:08:12,715 --> 00:08:14,237
None of that is dramatic.

306
00:08:14,237 --> 00:08:15,055
All of it was gone

307
00:08:15,055 --> 00:08:16,177
for two years.

308
00:08:16,177 --> 00:08:17,461
A few weeks later

309
00:08:17,461 --> 00:08:18,431
my husband asked if I

310
00:08:18,431 --> 00:08:19,563
wanted to walk the long

311
00:08:19,563 --> 00:08:20,952
way around the block.

312
00:08:20,952 --> 00:08:21,827
And for the first time

313
00:08:21,827 --> 00:08:22,969
in two years,

314
00:08:22,969 --> 00:08:24,132
I said yes.

315
00:08:24,900 --> 00:08:26,612
I wanted to understand
why,

316
00:08:26,612 --> 00:08:28,124
so I read the whole thing.

317
00:08:28,124 --> 00:08:30,151
It comes down to four
steps.

318
00:08:30,151 --> 00:08:30,978
One.

319
00:08:30,978 --> 00:08:32,462
The tissue around a new
knee can

320
00:08:32,462 --> 00:08:35,553
stay inflamed long after
surgery is over.

321
00:08:35,553 --> 00:08:36,279
Two.

322
00:08:36,828 --> 00:08:39,082
Inflamed tissue holds
extra fluid,

323
00:08:39,082 --> 00:08:39,967
so it takes up more

324
00:08:39,967 --> 00:08:41,185
room than it should.

325
00:08:41,185 --> 00:08:42,193
Three.

326
00:08:42,193 --> 00:08:43,820
There's only so much room
in there.

327
00:08:43,820 --> 00:08:45,189
Bending compresses it.

328
00:08:45,189 --> 00:08:46,781
Straightening pulls it
tight.

329
00:08:47,311 --> 00:08:48,823
That's the squeeze.

330
00:08:48,823 --> 00:08:49,606
Four.

331
00:08:50,136 --> 00:08:52,238
Red and near-infrared
light have been

332
00:08:52,238 --> 00:08:54,435
studied for calming that
inflammation,

333
00:08:54,435 --> 00:08:55,929
so the swelling and the
pressure

334
00:08:55,929 --> 00:08:57,441
can come down with it.

335
00:08:57,441 --> 00:08:59,058
In a randomized trial,

336
00:08:59,058 --> 00:09:00,827
patients given light
therapy after

337
00:09:00,827 --> 00:09:03,662
a knee replacement had
less pain,

338
00:09:03,662 --> 00:09:05,793
less swelling and better
early movement

339
00:09:05,793 --> 00:09:07,163
than those who weren't.

340
00:09:07,163 --> 00:09:09,921
A 2025 review said the
same,

341
00:09:09,921 --> 00:09:11,234
and was clear the evidence

342
00:09:11,234 --> 00:09:12,442
is still limited.

343
00:09:12,442 --> 00:09:13,869
I probably sound like a
broken

344
00:09:13,869 --> 00:09:15,419
record to my family.

345
00:09:15,419 --> 00:09:17,312
But after two years of
doing everything

346
00:09:17,312 --> 00:09:19,386
I was told and getting
nowhere,

347
00:09:19,386 --> 00:09:20,651
you have no idea what it's

348
00:09:20,651 --> 00:09:22,201
like to sleep through the
night,

349
00:09:22,201 --> 00:09:23,495
say yes to the walk,

350
00:09:23,495 --> 00:09:24,915
and get my life back.

351
00:09:25,340 --> 00:09:26,739
So take it from me.

352
00:09:26,739 --> 00:09:28,204
Don't spend another year
waiting

353
00:09:28,204 --> 00:09:29,383
